15. Victim-Centered Measurement

Traditional cybercrime measurement focuses on arrests, seizures, servers, wallets, markets, and revenue. DHO proposes an additional question:

\boxed{ \text{How much human harm was prevented?} }

The Australian Institute of Criminology's 2025 harm index demonstrates that cybercrime harm extends beyond direct financial loss and includes practical, health, social, financial, and legal consequences. DHO therefore evaluates intervention according to its effect on victims, not merely its effect on criminal infrastructure.

