21.2 Data Poisoning

Adversaries may attempt to poison training data by creating fake accounts with manipulated reputations, injecting false transactions, or generating misleading forum posts. Mitigations include robust aggregation (Krum, Trimmed Mean, or Median-based aggregation), anomaly detection to identify and exclude anomalous training samples, provenance verification to validate data sources, and manual inspection of suspicious data.

