22. Safety Boundary

The research architecture explicitly excludes: unauthorized access to systems; exploitation of darknet infrastructure; credential theft; malware deployment; deanonymization of ordinary users; mass surveillance; automated accusation; automated punishment; vigilante disruption; and publication of operational information that would facilitate criminal activity.

The research objective is:

\boxed{ \text{Detection} + \text{Understanding} + \text{Prevention} + \text{Victim Protection} }

rather than:

\boxed{ \text{Intrusion} + \text{Exposure} + \text{Punishment} }

These boundaries are enforced through technical controls (hard-coded restrictions on system capabilities), procedural controls (dual-key authorization, audit logs), institutional controls (ethics board oversight, independent audits), and legal controls (contractual obligations, regulatory compliance).

