B.3 Functional Operational State

Definition B.3.1 (Soft-Threshold Activation). The functional operational state \psi_j(t) \in [0,1] of node v_j is:

\psi_j(t) = \sigma\left( \sum_{l \in \mathcal{L}_{\text{edge}}} \beta_l S_{jl}(t) - \theta_j \right) \cdot \prod_{k \in \mathcal{D}_j^{\text{crit}}} \mathbb{I}(S_{jk}(t) > 0)

where:

S_{jl}(t) = \sum_{i \in \mathcal{N}_{\text{in}}^{(l)}(v_j,t)} w_{ij}^{(l)}(t) \psi_i(t)

and \sigma(x) = (1+e^{-x})^{-1}.

Lemma B.3.2. \psi_j(t) \in [0,1] for all j,t.

Proof. The logistic function \sigma: \mathbb{R} \to (0,1) maps any real input to the open interval (0,1). The indicator product is either 0 or 1. Therefore the product lies in [0,1). The boundary value 1 is attained in the limit as \sum_l \beta_l S_{jl} \to \infty, but for finite weights and bounded \psi_i, \psi_j < 1. \square

Proposition B.3.3 (Critical Dependency Gating). If any critical dependency layer k \in \mathcal{D}_j^{\text{crit}} has zero aggregate input, then \psi_j(t) = 0, regardless of all other dependencies.

Proof. If S_{jk}(t) = 0 for some k \in \mathcal{D}_j^{\text{crit}}, then \mathbb{I}(S_{jk}(t) > 0) = 0, and the product over critical layers is zero. The entire expression vanishes. \square

This captures the intuition that a marketplace cannot operate without payment processing or infrastructure, even if it has abundant listings and reputation.

