B.4 Ecosystem Resilience Metric

Definition B.4.1 (Continuous Resilience). For an intervention policy u over horizon T:

R_E(\mathcal{G},u) = \int_{t_0}^{t_0+T} \frac{\Phi(F(\mathcal{G}(t), u(t), a^*(t), \epsilon(t)))}{\Phi(\mathcal{G}(t_0))} \, dt

Definition B.4.2 (Discrete Operational Proxy). The discrete decomposition:

R_E = w_1 \mu(\mathcal{G}) + w_2 \frac{|\mathcal{S}_{\text{S2S}}(\mathcal{G})|}{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{vend}}|} + w_3 \exp(-\lambda_{\text{rec}} \tau_{\text{migration}})

with w_1 + w_2 + w_3 = 1, w_i \geq 0, is an operational proxy for the continuous integral, where:

· \mu(\mathcal{G}) = \frac{|\{v \in \mathcal{V}_{\text{vend}} : \deg_{\text{out}}^{(\text{market})}(v) \geq 2\}|}{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{vend}}|}
· |\mathcal{S}_{\text{S2S}}(\mathcal{G})| is the size of the seller-to-seller giant component in co-occurrence layers
· \tau_{\text{migration}} is the recovery half-life

Proposition B.4.3. R_E \in [0,1] under the discrete proxy.

Proof. Each term is bounded in [0,1]:

· \mu(\mathcal{G}) \in [0,1] by definition as a ratio of subset to total.
· \frac{|\mathcal{S}_{\text{S2S}}|}{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{vend}}|} \in [0,1] as a component-to-total ratio.
· \exp(-\lambda_{\text{rec}} \tau_{\text{migration}}) \in (0,1] for \lambda_{\text{rec}}, \tau_{\text{migration}} > 0.

With w_i \geq 0 and \sum w_i = 1, the weighted sum is a convex combination, hence in [0,1]. \square

Remark B.4.4. The continuous integral R_E \in [0,\infty) is unbounded above because \Phi can grow. The discrete proxy is a normalized operational approximation that trades theoretical generality for practical estimability.

