B.7 Differential Privacy Composition

Definition B.7.1 ((\varepsilon,\delta)-Differential Privacy). A randomized mechanism \mathcal{M} satisfies (\varepsilon,\delta)-DP if for any two neighboring datasets D, D' differing in one record, and any output set S:

P(\mathcal{M}(D) \in S) \leq e^\varepsilon P(\mathcal{M}(D') \in S) + \delta

Definition B.7.2 (Privacy Loss). For a mechanism \mathcal{M} and adjacent datasets D, D', the privacy loss random variable is:

\mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{M}(D) \| \mathcal{M}(D')}(o) = \log \frac{P(\mathcal{M}(D) = o)}{P(\mathcal{M}(D') = o)}

Definition B.7.3 (Moments Accountant). The moments accountant tracks:

\alpha_{\mathcal{M}}(l) = \max_{D, D'} \log \mathbb{E}_{o \sim \mathcal{M}(D)} \left[ \exp\left( l \cdot \mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{M}(D) \| \mathcal{M}(D')}(o) \right) \right]

for integer l.

Theorem B.7.4 (Composability). Suppose \mathcal{M} consists of adaptive mechanisms \mathcal{M}_1, \ldots, \mathcal{M}_m. Then:

\alpha_{\mathcal{M}}(l) \leq \sum_{i=1}^m \alpha_{\mathcal{M}_i}(l)



Theorem B.7.5 ((\varepsilon,\delta) from Moments). For any \delta > 0, \mathcal{M} is (\varepsilon,\delta)-DP for:

\varepsilon = \min_l \frac{\alpha_{\mathcal{M}}(l) + \log(1/\delta)}{l}



Proposition B.7.6 (Federated Composition). For n institutions each running a (\varepsilon_i, \delta_i)-DP local mechanism, the global mechanism satisfies:

\varepsilon_{\text{global}} \leq \sum_{i=1}^n \varepsilon_i, \quad \delta_{\text{global}} \leq \sum_{i=1}^n \delta_i

Proof. Direct application of Theorem B.7.4 and B.7.5 with adaptive composition over institutions. \square

